course: dictionary
lesson: 8913
title: One word, many meanings: sick
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word sick can mean different things. The words around it show you which meaning is right. «He felt sick.» Here sick means ill, not healthy. You might feel sick with a fever, a cough or a sore throat.
explain: Sick can also mean to throw up food from your stomach. «A boy in Scotland ate shiny red berries from a bush in the park; he was sick and dizzy.» The words dizzy and rush him to hospital tell you this is about being ill, not about being bored.
explain: Sick can mean bored or annoyed because there has been too much of something. «I am sick of rain» means I have had too much rain and I want it to stop. In slang, sick can even mean very cool or great. Ask yourself: what does this word mean in this sentence?
fact: Sick means ill, not healthy.
fact: Sick can mean to throw up food from your stomach. In the UK, the noun sick means vomit.
fact: Sick of something means bored or annoyed with it because there has been too much of it.
fact: Phrases with sick include feel sick, off sick, sick day, carsick, seasick, homesick and sick and tired.
fact: When you are sick, wash your hands and stay home, because germs spread.
exercise: «He felt sick.» What does sick mean here? | *Ill, not healthy | Very cool and great | Bored with too much of something | Strong and fit
exercise: «A boy ate shiny red berries; he was sick and dizzy.» What does sick mean here? | Healthy and full of energy | Very cool | Bored of the park | *Threw up food from his stomach
exercise: Jade says, «The new skate park is sick!» What does sick mean here? | Ill in bed | Throwing up | Bored and annoyed | *Very cool or great
test: Sick of something means? | *Bored or annoyed because there has been too much of it | Ill with a fever | Living on a ship | Very cool and great
test: In «Heat exhaustion can turn into heatstroke; one warning sign is that a hot person stops sweating», what is the warning sign? | The person grows taller | The person starts singing | *The person stops sweating | The person smiles more
exam: Which meaning fits sick in carsick? | *Feeling ill because of moving in a car | Very cool car | Bored of cars | Healthy after a long drive
